  "IntegrationModelHealthObservation": {
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "definitions": {
      "IntegrationModelHealthState": {
        "enum": [
          "unknown",
          "healthy",
          "cooling_down",
          "needs_configuration",
          "probing",
          "interrupted"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      },
      "ProviderFailureCategory": {
        "enum": [
          "authentication_error",
          "forbidden",
          "model_or_route",
          "invalid_parameter",
          "context_length_exceeded",
          "rate_limit",
          "quota_exceeded",
          "network_error",
          "timeout_error",
          "model_protocol_error",
          "provider_error"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      },
      "ProviderFailureDetails": {
        "description": "Allowlisted terminal facts, independent of the provider's diagnostic text.\n\nThree different questions are answered here, and a consumer must not collapse them into one \"can I retry?\" flag:\n\n- [`Self::retryable`] — repeating the *request* is allowed. It says nothing about whether the failed attempt already produced visible output. - [`Self::resume_safe`] — repeating it cannot duplicate a response that had already started streaming, so the conversation can be resumed as it stands. - [`Self::recovery_action`] — whether a human has to act at all.\n\nNone of them means \"this failed turn can be continued from its committed boundary\": that is a separate server capability (`kcoder_app_protocol::CAPABILITY_FAILED_TURN_CONTINUATION_V1`, requested with `turn/start.retryFromTurnId`), and a client must gate on the capability rather than infer it from these booleans.",
        "properties": {
          "category": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/ProviderFailureCategory"
          },
          "http_status": {
            "format": "uint16",
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "recovery_action": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/ProviderFailureRecoveryAction"
          },
          "resume_safe": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "retry_after_ms": {
            "format": "uint64",
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "retryable": {
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "category",
          "recovery_action",
          "resume_safe",
          "retryable"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ProviderFailureRecoveryAction": {
        "description": "Terminal instructions never schedule another invocation or approval request.",
        "enum": [
          "needs_human",
          "diagnose_only"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "properties": {
      "configurationRevision": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "consecutiveFailures": {
        "format": "uint32",
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "cooldownUntil": {
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "failure": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/ProviderFailureDetails"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      },
      "lastObservedAt": {
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "model": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "provider": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "responseStarted": {
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "state": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/IntegrationModelHealthState"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "configurationRevision",
      "consecutiveFailures",
      "model",
      "provider",
      "responseStarted",
      "state"
    ],
    "title": "IntegrationModelHealthObservation",
    "type": "object"
  },
